@lang en
IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `nii-il33-nouns`

-- ===========================================================================
-- The readings this row takes where the text does not decide. Row IL-33.
--
-- RULED by Meng on 2026-10-08 (SHRUG, applying to every ambiguity): where the text is silent or two
-- readings are arguable and give different answers to a question someone would ask, one named switch,
-- default DECLINE (a refusal by name saying the text does not decide), the other readings kept by name
-- and tested; the default declines ONLY where the readings give different answers to the question
-- asked. Each switch below is one field of one record; `the readings this row takes` is the default.
-- A setter per field returns the record with that one field changed, for a caller or a test that wants
-- a reading by name.
-- ===========================================================================

§ `The readings`

GIVETH A `The readings this row takes where the text does not decide`
`the readings this row takes` MEANS
    `The readings this row takes where the text does not decide` WITH
        `the day an age is reached` IS `age: such a day is declined`
        `exactly 183 days in section 2A` IS `exactly 183 days is declined where the readings differ`
        `the words sits in Israel in section 65(a)` IS `the words sit in Israel are declined where section 2A would exclude a person who in fact lives in Israel`
        `a self-employed person who works outside Israel` IS `declined where the two readings differ`
        `the word married in the definition of a housewife` IS `the word married is declined for a woman known in public as the wife`
        `the maintenance limb of the definition of a widow` IS `the grammar of the maintenance limb is declined where the two readings differ`
        `section 71 where both parents died or ceased to be insured` IS `section 71 is declined where the readings differ`
        `a request under section 69(b) and a decision under section 69(d)` IS `declined where the two differ`
        `a fall in the index, in the updating clause of the basic amount` IS `a fall in the index is declined where the two readings differ`
        `a month in which the period of payment begins or ends partway` IS `a month in which the period begins or ends partway is declined where the two readings differ`
        `the child allowance and the supplement of section 68(c), for rounding` IS `rounding is declined where the two readings differ`
        `a child as in section 68(b), for section 69A(1)` IS `declined where the two readings differ`

@ref Meng's ruling of 2026-10-08 (SHRUG)
GIVEN rd IS A `The readings this row takes where the text does not decide`
      x  IS A `A reading of the day an age is reached where the later month lacks the day of birth`
GIVETH A `The readings this row takes where the text does not decide`
`the readings` rd `with` `the day an age is reached` `read as` x MEANS
    `The readings this row takes where the text does not decide` WITH
        `the day an age is reached` IS x
        `exactly 183 days in section 2A` IS rd's `exactly 183 days in section 2A`
        `the words sits in Israel in section 65(a)` IS rd's `the words sits in Israel in section 65(a)`
        `a self-employed person who works outside Israel` IS rd's `a self-employed person who works outside Israel`
        `the word married in the definition of a housewife` IS rd's `the word married in the definition of a housewife`
        `the maintenance limb of the definition of a widow` IS rd's `the maintenance limb of the definition of a widow`
        `section 71 where both parents died or ceased to be insured` IS rd's `section 71 where both parents died or ceased to be insured`
        `a request under section 69(b) and a decision under section 69(d)` IS rd's `a request under section 69(b) and a decision under section 69(d)`
        `a fall in the index, in the updating clause of the basic amount` IS rd's `a fall in the index, in the updating clause of the basic amount`
        `a month in which the period of payment begins or ends partway` IS rd's `a month in which the period of payment begins or ends partway`
        `the child allowance and the supplement of section 68(c), for rounding` IS rd's `the child allowance and the supplement of section 68(c), for rounding`
        `a child as in section 68(b), for section 69A(1)` IS rd's `a child as in section 68(b), for section 69A(1)`

@ref Meng's ruling of 2026-10-08 (SHRUG)
